steps.response:
The provided image is a lateral chest X-ray ("LT LAT"). To distinguish between right and left lower lobe atelectasis on a lateral view, one must identify the location of the opacity relative to the oblique fissures and the spine. Right lower lobe atelectasis typically presents as a triangular opacity overlying the lower thoracic spine with loss of the posterior hemidiaphragm contour. Left lower lobe atelectasis often appears as increased density behind the heart or along the posterior spine.

I will use `chest_xray_expert` to get a focused interpretation of this lateral view to determine the side of the atelectasis.

